# Example client authorization file for TOR
# This file shows the correct format for Tor hidden service client authorization
#
## TOR SETUP: Client side
# To access a version 3 Onion Service with client authorization as a client,
#  make sure you have ClientOnionAuthDir set in your torrc.
#
# For example, add this line to /etc/tor/torrc:
# ClientOnionAuthDir /var/lib/tor/onion_auth
#
# sudo mkdir /var/lib/tor/onion_auth
# sudo chown debian-tor /var/lib/tor/onion_auth
# sudo chmod 700 /var/lib/tor/onion_auth
#
# Then, in the <ClientOnionAuthDir> directory, create an .auth_private file for the Onion Service corresponding to this key
# (i.e. 'bob_onion.auth_private').
# The content of the <ClientOnionAuthDir>/<user>.auth_private file should look like this Format:
#
# <56-char-onion-addr-without-.onion>:descriptor:x25519:<52-char-private-key>
#
# Example (this is a dummy key, replace with your actual keys):
# peannyjkqwqfynd24p6dszvtchkq7hfkwymi5by5y332wmosy5dwfaqd:descriptor:x25519:ZDUVQQ7IKBXSGR2WWOBNM3VP5ELNOYSSINDK7CAUN2WD7A3EKZWQ
